itecture School of Business Administration School of Education School of Indigenous Relations School of Kinesiology and Health Sciences School of Liberal Arts School of Natural Sciences School of Nursing School of Social Sciences School of Social Work School of Speech-Language Pathology School of Sports Administration Close Services Our services and support are here to help you succeed in your studies and experience university life to the fullest. View all services Menu Parking Residence myLaurentian Hub Academic Support International Students Services Athletics and Campus Rec Campus Life Doing Business with Laurentian Equity, Diversity and Human Rights Health and Wellbeing Academic Support Academic Advising Accessibility Services Bookstore Indigenous Student Affairs Library & Archives myLaurentianHub Peer Programs Research Services The Virtual Backpack Jim Fielding Innovation & Commercialization Space International Students Services Current International Students Newly Admitted International Students Health Insurance Work in Canada Study in Canada Outgoing Exchange Students Incoming Exchange Students Travel Requirements Athletics and Campus Rec Athletics Campus Recreation Campus Life Apparel Store Campus Safety Clubs Daycare Employment Services Indigenous Student Affairs International Exchange Program IT Services Meal Plans and Eating on Campus Orientation Parking Peer Programs Residence Study Abroad Student Associations Student Equity Centre The Student Success Centre Student Equity Centre Student Equity Centre About Us Events & Initiatives Pride Women's Centre Doing Business with Laurentian Business Services Conference and Event Services Printing Services Equity, Diversity and Human Rights Office of Equity, Diversity and Human Rights Accessibility Policy Anti-Racism & Anti-Hate Black History Month Prevention and Response to Sexual Violence Health and Wellbeing Counselling Laurentian Re-U Free Store Laurentian University Food Bank Medical Clinic Mental Health & Wellness Support Services Speech and Language Clinic Close About Laurentian University Learn about Laurentian University’s mission, leadership, and initiatives. Learn about Laurentian University Menu News Careers Contact Us Campus Maps Governance & Leadership Policies & Accountability Office of Sustainability Facts & Figures News News Social Media Events Student Stories Careers Careers Administrative Vacancies Faculty Vacancies Governance & Leadership Governance & Leadership Board of Governors Chancellor General Counsel LUNEC Leadership Planning President Senate President Listening Tour Policies & Accountability Policies & Accountability Finance and Budget Academic Accountability AODA at Laurentian University Copyright Notice of Collection Policies Policy on the Freedom of Speech Procurement and Contracts Purchasing Policy Office of Sustainability Office of Sustainability Laurentian Greenspace Global Lessons from the Restoration Story of Sudbury, Canada Laurentian's Nature Positive University Close Information for... Menu Future Students Future International Students Current Students Current International Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents & Counselors Donors Close Research Learn more about Research at Laurentian University Menu Research Research Centres Research Chairs & Fellows Funding Opportunities Highlights Our People Strategic Research Plan Animal Care and Lab-Bio Safety Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Ethics Intellectual Property & Commercialization Jim Fielding Innovation Space ROMEO Research Data Management Research Support Fund Qualtrics Menu Search Home About Laurentian Office of Sustainability Laurentian is a Nature Positive University Laurentian is a Nature Positive University Addressing the impacts and influence of our institution on nature Lire la version française Overview Laurentian University is committed to the global Nature Positive University Alliance (NPUA) pledge by implementing meaningful biodiversity conservation initiatives, engaging students and the broader community, and enhancing institutional sustainability efforts. Mission Statement Our Nature Positive University (NPU) is committed to protecting, restoring, and celebrating biodiversity while fostering global leadership in finding environmental solutions. As a recognized NPU, Laurentian University joins a network of over 730 institutions across 106 countries working collectively to address the climate and biodiversity crises, enhance student engagement, and strengthen institutional reputation. Greenspace Read more about Greenspace Biodiversity at Laurentian University Read more about Biodiversity at Laurentian University Nature Positive Projects Read more about Nature Positive Projects Our Team A dedicated and passionate team of students, staff, and faculty, all united by a shared commitment to environmental sustainability and positive change. Global Nature Positive Universities Year in Review 2025 (PDF) Read more 2024 (PDF) Read more 2023 (PDF) Read more 2022 (PDF) Read more Get Involved Interested in getting involved and making a difference? We’d love to hear from you! Whether you’re a student, faculty, or staff member, there are countless opportunities to contribute to our mission of fostering a nature-positive future. Email us today to learn more about how you can be part of our passionate team and help drive meaningful change. Together, we can make a lasting impact! Email Press Releases Laurentian University joining Nature Positive Universities Alliance Housed at the Vale Living with Lakes Centre Office: LL 114 environment@laurentian.ca 840 Ramsey Lake Rd Greater Sudbury, ON P3E 6H5 Stay connected and never miss an update! Follow us on social media for the latest news! Facebook Instagram Make an Impact Send a donation to the Laurentian Nature Positive University team today Donate Laurentian University 1.800.461.4030 705.675.1151 935 Ramsey Lake Road, Sudbury, ON P3E 2C6 Contact Us Social Media Visits and Tours Report a problem with the website Are You Okay? Accessibility Services Careers Directories Helpful Contacts News Land Acknowledgment - Aki Gaabijidebendaagwak We would like to acknowledge the Robinson-Huron Treaty of 1850. We also further recognize that Laurentian University is located on the traditional lands of the Atikameksheng Anishnawbek and that the City of Greater Sudbury, also includes the traditional lands of the Wahnapitae First Nation. We extend our deepest respect to Indigenous peoples - as a sign of our continued relationship we will support Laurentian University ’s Truth and Reconciliation Task Force Recommendations. Miigwech. Listen to it in Anishinaabemowin . Privacy Policy Accessibility Policy Sitemap Laurentian University. Sudbury, Ontario, Canada. All Rights Reserved. 2026 Close"
